From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yue Gao <yuega2@cisco.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vlib: wake sleeping workers in vlib_worker_wait_one_loop

vlib_worker_wait_one_loop() spins until every worker has been once
around its main loop, but never wakes them. A worker with no polling
input node sleeps in epoll for up to 10 ms, so the main thread spins
until the timeout expires. FIB calls it on every route uninstall, so
with interrupt or adaptive rx-mode each route delete costs up to 10 ms
(~100 deletes/s), while adds are unaffected.

Wake each worker while waiting for it. vlib_thread_wakeup() only writes
the eventfd when the worker has announced it is sleeping, so calling it
inside the spin also covers a worker that goes to sleep after the wait
starts.

Type: fix

diff --git a/src/vlib/threads.c b/src/vlib/threads.c
index c7ed41bd6..dc1244514 100644
--- a/src/vlib/threads.c
+++ b/src/vlib/threads.c
@@ -1618,6 +1618,9 @@ vlib_worker_wait_one_loop (void)
 	   * so at least one worker cannot make any progress */
 	  if (vlib_worker_threads->wait_before_barrier)
 	    break;
+	  /* a worker sleeping in epoll would otherwise only come round
+	   * when its timeout expires */
+	  vlib_thread_wakeup (ii);
 	  CLIB_PAUSE ();
 	}
     }
